    "body": "Stacked on #46245 (FFN residual chain), #46244 and #46228; review the commits after #46245.\n\n## Motivation\n\nEach Wan block projects the 512 text tokens to the cross-attention K and V (and RMS-normalizes K) in every denoising step: on Wan2.2 A14B 720p (4xB300) two small GEMMs and a norm, ~0.07 ms of every block, 40 blocks x 40 steps. The text and the DiT weights do not change inside a denoising loop, and the denoising stage hands the transformer the same prompt-embedding tensor at every step of the loop (the CFG branch kwargs are built once per loop). LTX-2 does the same per loop in #46105 through its own denoising stage. Wan runs the shared stage, so the transformer keys the projection by the prompt tensor, and the shared stage frees it when the loop ends.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`managers/forward_context.py`: `DENOISING_LOOP_STATE`, a `Req.extra` key for what models keep for one denoising loop. Its leading `_` keeps it out of disaggregated request transfers, like `_skip_softmax_params`.\n\n`pipelines_core/stages/denoising.py`: `_post_denoising_loop` drops it. The standard, progressive, DMD and LTX-2 loops all end there, before decode. The stage knows nothing about what is inside, so there is no per-model hook and no getattr/hasattr fallback.\n\n`models/dits/wanvideo.py`:\n- `WanT2VCrossAttention.project_context_kv(context)` returns the normed K and the V that `forward` projects; `forward(..., context_kv=None)` uses them when given.\n- `WanTransformerBlock.forward(..., text_kv=None)` passes them to `attn2`.\n- `WanTransformer3DModel._text_kvs(source, context)`: on the first step with a prompt tensor `source`, it projects every block's K/V from the embedded `context`. They are stored in the forward context's request, under `req.extra[DENOISING_LOOP_STATE]`, keyed by `(id(model), id(source))`. The entry holds `source` so its id cannot be reused while cached. The module holds none of them: they go when the loop ends and never outlive the request, throug